From 5a03ebf75d4ef2dd1c78675f4d986ef9d851e4e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:47:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(spec-decode): profile adaptive verification on distinct
 real rows

Adaptive verification prices draft budgets from a startup profile of dummy
batches. Every dummy row repeats token 0 and is marked as padding, which
the MoE routers skip (VLLM_MOE_SKIP_PADDING), so the profile leaves out the
routed-expert work, the cost that grows with every verification row: the
tables price a verified row at about 0.4 ms against several milliseconds
in real decode steps.

With SPARK3_DSPARK_PROFILE_TOKENS=random the cost profile runs on a fixed
pseudo-random token sequence (seed 0, identical on every rank), marked as
real rows, and on the embeddings of those tokens where the model takes
inputs_embeds. InputBatch.make_dummy copies the ids and clears the padding
flag only while they are set. Graph capture and every other dummy run are
unchanged; the embedding buffer is restored afterwards. Output is
unchanged.
